A :RESUME in a procedure with no :ERROR does not compile:
error_handler_structure on the :RESUME, plus its deprecated_keyword
warning (diag.error_handler_structure fourth Flags fence).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE StoreAudit;
	:PARAMETERS sAction;
	RunSQL("INSERT INTO AUDITLOG(ACTION) VALUES(?)",, {sAction});
	:RESUME;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE StoreAudit;
	:PARAMETERS sAction;
	RunSQL("INSERT INTO AUDITLOG(ACTION) VALUES(?)",, {sAction});
	:RESUME;
	:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:2-4:9 warning deprecated_keyword: ':RESUME' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
4:2-4:9 error error_handler_structure: ':RESUME' without an ':ERROR' handler in the same procedure does not compile
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:2-4:9 warning deprecated_keyword: ':RESUME' is legacy error handling. Prefer ':TRY' / ':CATCH' / ':FINALLY'
4:2-4:9 error error_handler_structure: ':RESUME' without an ':ERROR' handler in the same procedure does not compile
